:Class Stark
⍝ THIS PROJECT IS NOT FOR PUBLIC USE YET
⍝ IT HAS NOT YET BEEN THOROUGHLY REVIEWED
⍝ THIS PROJECT IS IN A BETA PHASE

⍝ Fastify-style HTTP router for Dyalog APL, built on top of Jarvis.
⍝
⍝ Usage:
⍝   ⍝ First define your functions, ListUsers, and GetUser, and CreateUser
⍝   router←Stark.New ()
⍝   ⍝ Matrix mode (method path handler options per row):
⍝   router.Register [
⍝       'GET'  '/users'       'ListUsers'   ()
⍝       'GET'  '/users/{id}'  'GetUser'     ()
⍝       'POST' '/users'       'CreateUser'  opts   ⍝ opts is a namespace with metadata
⍝   ]
⍝   ⍝ Namespace vector mode (.method .path .handler, and optionally .spec):
⍝   router.Register (
⍝       (method: 'GET'  ⋄ path: '/users'      ⋄ handler: 'ListUsers')
⍝       (method: 'GET'  ⋄ path: '/users/{id}' ⋄ handler: 'GetUser')
⍝       (method: 'POST' ⋄ path: '/users'      ⋄ handler: 'CreateUser' ⋄ spec: opts)
⍝   )
⍝   router.Start 8080

    :Field Public  Handlers      ⍝ namespace where handler functions live
    :Field Public  ThreadMode←'' ⍝ DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD: '' (Jarvis default), 0, 1, 'DEBUG', 'AUTO'
    :Field Public  Info          ⍝ namespace with title, version, description for OpenAPI info
    :Field Public  Spec←()       ⍝ additional root-level OpenAPI fields (components, security, servers, etc.)
    :Field Public  Debug←0       ⍝ 0=all errors trapped, 1=stop on error in dispatch, 2=stop before user handler, 4=Jarvis framework debug, 8=Conga event logging, 16=stop before response, 32=Stark framework debug, 64=stop before routing
    :Field Public  OnErrorFn←''  ⍝ if set, called as err OnErrorFn req after Fail 500 instead of resignalling; err is a ⎕DMX clone
    :Field Public  OnFailFn←''   ⍝ if set, called as fail OnFailFn req to build the body of Stark's own 401/403/404/405 responses
    :Field Public  OnRequestFn←'' ⍝ if set, called as OnRequestFn req before routing; req.Fail with an error status turns the request away
    :Field Public  OnResponseFn←'' ⍝ if set, called as result OnResponseFn req once the response is known; observes only
    :Field Public  DocsSecurity←⍬ ⍝ security requirement for /openapi.json; ⍬ = public
    :Field Private _routes       ⍝ vector of route descriptor namespaces
    :Field Private _jarvis       ⍝ underlying Jarvis instance
    :Field Private _security     ⍝ N×3 matrix of (scheme name, OpenAPI scheme definition, hook name)

    ∇ Make0
      :Access Public
      :Implements Constructor
      Info←(title: 'AStarkAPI' ⋄ version: '1.0.0')
      Spec←()
      Handlers←1(86⌶)'⎕THIS'
      _routes←0 4⍴''
      _security←0 3⍴''
      _jarvis←⎕NEW (⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS).##.Jarvis
      '/openapi.json' Get '_OpenAPIHandler'
    ∇

    ∇ inst←New args
      :Access Public Shared
      inst←⎕NEW ⎕THIS
      inst.Handlers←1(86⌶)'⎕THIS'
    ∇

    ⍝ Route registration
    ⍝ path router.Get 'HandlerName'
    ⍝ path router.Get ('HandlerName' opts)

    ∇ {r}←path Get rarg
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_Register 'GET' path rarg
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←path Post rarg
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_Register 'POST' path rarg
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←path Put rarg
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_Register 'PUT' path rarg
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←path Delete rarg
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_Register 'DELETE' path rarg
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←path Patch rarg
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_Register 'PATCH' path rarg
    ∇


    ∇ {r}←_Register(method path rarg);handler;options;norm;existing
      :Access Private Instance
      :If 1≠≡rarg                           ⍝ nested: ('HandlerName' options)
          (handler options)←rarg
      :ElseIf ⍕⍛≡rarg
          handler←rarg                     ⍝ simple string
          options←()
      :Else
        ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: Right argument to Register must be a string (handler name) or a 2-element vector (handler name, options)'))
      :EndIf
      ⍝ Check for duplicate routes: normalize {param} segments so {id} and {user_id} match
      norm←_NormalizePath path
      :If 0<≢_routes
          existing←(_routes[;1]∊⍥⎕C ⊂method)⌿_routes
          :If 0<≢existing
              :If (⊂norm)∊_NormalizePath¨existing[;2]
                  ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: Duplicate route: ',method,' ',path,' conflicts with an existing registration'))
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
      r←method (,path) handler (_BuildOp method (,path) handler options)
      _routes⍪←r
    ∇

    ∇ {r}←Register routes;old;row;ns
      :Access Public
      ⍝ Matrix mode:    N×3 or N×4 matrix of (method path handler [spec])
      ⍝ Namespace mode: vector of namespaces, each with .method .path .handler and optionally .spec
      ⍝ Every route goes through _Register's duplicate check; if any route is rejected, none are registered
      old←_routes
      :Trap 0
          :If 2=⍴⍴routes
              :For row :In ↓routes
                  _Register(1⊃row)(2⊃row)((3⊃row)(4⊃row,⊂()))
              :EndFor
          :Else
              :For ns :In ,routes
                  :If 9=ns.⎕NC'spec'
                      _Register ns.method ns.path(ns.handler ns.spec)
                  :Else
                      _Register ns.method ns.path ns.handler
                  :EndIf
              :EndFor
          :EndIf
      :Else
          _routes←old
          ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.(('EN'EN)('Message'Message))
      :EndTrap
      r←Routes
    ∇

    ⍝ Cover function for 7162⌶ (mangle string into valid APL name)
    _Mangle←{0(7162⌶)⍵}

    ⍝ Replace {param} segments with a placeholder and drop empty segments, so paths that
    ⍝ pathMatch treats as identical (/items/{id}, /items/{item_id}, /items/{id}/) compare equal
    _NormalizePath←{∊'/',¨{'{'=⊃⍵:'{}' ⋄ ⍵}¨'/'(≠⊆⊢),⍵}

    ∇ op←_BuildOp r;method;path;handler;opts;segs;varMask;param;pNS;pathParams;names;user;over;pairs
      :Access Private Instance
      (method path handler opts)←r

      op←(responses: ())
      op.operationId←handler

      segs←'/'(≠⊆⊢)path
      varMask←'{'=⊃¨segs
      pathParams←⍬
      names←{1↓¯1↓⍵}¨varMask/segs
      :For param :In names
          pathParams,←⊂(name: param ⋄ in: 'path' ⋄ required: (⊂'true') ⋄ schema: (type: 'string'))
      :EndFor

      :If 9=⎕NC'opts'
          op ⎕NS opts                           ⍝ merge — user's OpenAPI fields pass through
                                                ⍝ note: if opts had parameters, ⎕NS just copied it; we overwrite below
          op.parameters←pathParams              ⍝ path params first, then append user-supplied extras
          :If 2≤opts.⎕NC'parameters'
              user←,opts.parameters
              over←{6::'' ⋄ 'path'≡⍵.in:⍵.name ⋄ ''}¨user
              op.parameters←((~names∊over)/pathParams),user   ⍝ a user path param replaces the generated one of the same name
          :EndIf

          :If 2≤opts.⎕NC'responses'
              :If ~(9.1=42∘⎕ATX)'opts.responses'
                  pairs←,⊆opts.responses        ⍝ shorthand: vector of (statusCode schema) pairs
                  :If 0=≡⊃pairs ⋄ pairs←,⊂pairs ⋄ :EndIf  ⍝ a single pair such as (204 ⍬)
                  op.responses←()
                  op.responses ⎕VSET ↓⍉↑(_Mangle∘⍕¨⊃¨pairs)((⊃¨pairs)_Response¨(2⊃¨pairs))
              :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :Else
          op.parameters←pathParams
      :EndIf

      :If 0=≢op.parameters ⋄ op.⎕EX'parameters' ⋄ :EndIf

      :If 0=≢op.responses.⎕NL ¯2 ¯9
          op.responses ⎕VSET ⊂(_Mangle'200') (description: 'Successful response')
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ Expand one responses-shorthand pair into an OpenAPI Response Object:
    ⍝ description from the HTTP status text, schema (if a namespace) under application/json
    ∇ resp←code _Response schema;status
      status←(⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS).##.Jarvis.Request.HttpStatus
      resp←(description:(status[;1]⍳⊂code)⊃status[;2],⊂'Response')
      :If 9=⎕NC'schema'
          resp.content←(⍙application⍙47⍙json:(schema:schema))
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ∇ r←{value}DebugLevel level
    ⍝ monadic: return 1 if level is within Debug (powers of 2)
    ⍝ dyadic:  return value unless level is within Debug
      r←∨/((7⍴2)⊤⊃Debug)∨.∧(7⍴2)⊤level
      :If 0≠⎕NC'value'
          r←value/⍨~r
      :EndIf
    ∇

    stopIf←{1∊⍵:-⎕TRAP←0 'C' '⎕←''Stopped for debugging... (Press Ctrl-Enter)''' ⋄ shy←0}

    ⍝ pattern pathMatch path → (matched pathParams)
    pathMatch←{
        patSplit pathSplit←'/'(≠⊆⊢)¨⍺ ⍵
        pathSplit≢⍥≢patSplit:0()
        varMask←'{'=⊃¨patSplit
        ≢/(⊂~varMask)/¨patSplit pathSplit:0()
        names←({1↓¯1↓⍵}¨patSplit[⍸varMask])
        1(()⎕VSET↓⍉↑(0(7162⌶)names)(pathSplit[⍸varMask]))
    }

    ⍝ Entry point for every Jarvis request: routing (_Route), then OnResponseFn
    ∇ result←_Dispatch req;sig
      :Access Public Instance
      stopIf DebugLevel 64                          ⍝ stop before routing
      req.Route←''
      :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1                          ⍝ only errors Stark re-signals get here
          result←_Route req
      :Else
          sig←⊂⎕DMX.(('EN'EN)('EM'EM)('Message'(OSError{⍵,2⌽(×≢⊃⍬⍴2⌽⍺,⊂'')/'") ("',⊃⍬⍴2⌽⍺}Message)))
          req.Fail 500
          ⍬ _OnResponse req                         ⍝ log it before Jarvis turns it into a 500
          ⎕SIGNAL sig
      :EndTrap
      result _OnResponse req
    ∇

    ⍝ OnRequestFn, then route the request to the matching handler
    ∇ result←_Route req;r;pp;m;i;ok;allow;status
      :If ~0∊⍴OnRequestFn
          :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1             ⍝ disable trap if bit 1 set (stop on error)
              OnRequestFn _Ignore req
          :Else
              result←_HandleError req ⋄ :Return
          :EndTrap
          :If 400≤status←req.Response.Status        ⍝ OnRequestFn turned the request away
              result←(status: status ⋄ reason: 'blocked' ⋄ body: (detail: _StatusText status))_FailBody req
              :Return
          :EndIf
      :EndIf
      m pp←↓⍉↑_routes[;2] pathMatch¨⊂req.Endpoint
      :If ~∨/m                                      ⍝ no route has this path
          req.Fail 404
          result←(status: 404 ⋄ reason: 'not_found' ⋄ body: (detail: 'Not Found'))_FailBody req
          :Return
      :EndIf
      r←m⌿_routes ⋄ pp←m/pp
      :If ~∨/i←r[;1]∊⍥⎕C⊂req.Method                 ⍝ the path exists, but not for this method
          req.Fail 405
          allow←∪1 ⎕C r[;1]
          'Allow'req.SetHeader ¯2↓∊allow,¨⊂', '
          result←(status: 405 ⋄ reason: 'method_not_allowed' ⋄ body: (detail: 'Method Not Allowed'))_FailBody req
          :Return
      :EndIf
      r←i⌿r ⋄ pp←i/pp
      ⍝ Several patterns can match (/items/special and /items/{id}); prefer literal
      ⍝ segments over {param} ones, comparing left to right
      i←⊃⍋↑{'{'=⊃¨'/'(≠⊆⊢)⍵}¨r[;2]
      r←r[i;]
      req.Route←2⊃r
      req.PathParams←i⊃pp
      req.QueryParams←() ⎕VSET ↓{⍵≡0 2⍴⍬:0 2⍴⍬⋄n←⍵⋄n[;1]←0(7162⌶)n[;1]⋄n}req.QueryParams
      :If DebugLevel 32
      :AndIf '_'≠⊃3⊃r
          ⎕←'STARK: ',req.Method,' ',req.Endpoint,' → ',3⊃r
      :EndIf
      :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1                 ⍝ disable trap if bit 1 set (stop on error)
          (ok result)←r _Authenticate req
      :Else
          result←_HandleError req ⋄ :Return
      :EndTrap
      →ok↓0
      :If '_'=⊃3⊃r
          result←(⍎3⊃r)req          ⍝ internal handler (on Stark)
      :Else
          stopIf DebugLevel 2              ⍝ stop before user handler
          :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1             ⍝ disable trap if bit 1 set (stop on error)
              result←(Handlers⍎3⊃r)req
          :Else
              result←_HandleError req
          :EndTrap
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ Call OnResponseFn, if set, with the response body; an error in it is reported and otherwise ignored
    ∇ result _OnResponse req
      →0⍴⍨0∊⍴OnResponseFn
      :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1
          result(OnResponseFn _Ignore)req            ⍝ parenthesised: result OnResponseFn would strand as the operand
      :Else
          ⎕←'STARK: error in OnResponseFn "',OnResponseFn,'" (ignored): ',⎕DMX.(EM,(0<≢Message)/': ',Message)
      :EndTrap
    ∇

    ⍝ Call the Handlers function fn, monadically or dyadically, ignoring any result
    ∇ {larg}(fn _Ignore)rarg
      :If 0=⎕NC'larg'
          :If 0=10 Handlers.⎕ATX fn ⋄ (Handlers⍎fn)rarg ⋄ :Else ⋄ {}(Handlers⍎fn)rarg ⋄ :EndIf
      :Else
          :If 0=10 Handlers.⎕ATX fn ⋄ larg(Handlers⍎fn)rarg ⋄ :Else ⋄ {}larg(Handlers⍎fn)rarg ⋄ :EndIf
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ Standard HTTP status text, e.g. 'Forbidden' for 403
    _StatusText←{t←(⊃⊃⎕CLASS ⎕THIS).##.Jarvis.Request.HttpStatus ⋄ (t[;1]⍳⍵)⊃t[;2],⊂'Error'}

    ⍝ Handle an error trapped in a hook or handler: call OnErrorFn if set, otherwise resignal
    ∇ result←_HandleError req;err
      :If ~0∊⍴OnErrorFn
          err←()⎕NS ⎕DMX          ⍝ deep clone ⎕DMX before req.Fail may alter it
          req.Fail 500
          result←err(Handlers⍎OnErrorFn)req
      :Else
          ⎕SIGNAL⊂⎕DMX.(('EN'EN)('EM'EM)('Message'(OSError{⍵,2⌽(×≢⊃⍬⍴2⌽⍺,⊂'')/'") ("',⊃⍬⍴2⌽⍺}Message))) ⍝ RESIGNAL
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ Authentication
    ⍝ router.AddSecurity 'bearerAuth' (type:'http' ⋄ scheme:'bearer') 'CheckBearer'
    ⍝ Registers an OpenAPI security scheme and the Handlers function that checks it.
    ⍝ The hook is called as  user←auth Hook req  where auth has .scheme .credential .scopes;
    ⍝ it returns the authenticated user (any value but 0) or 0 to reject.

    ∇ AddSecurity(name definition hook)
      :Access Public Instance
      :If (⊂,name)∊_security[;1]
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: Security scheme "',name,'" is already registered'))
      :EndIf
      _security⍪←(,name) definition (,hook)
    ∇

    ⍝ The security requirement that applies to a route, as a vector of requirement namespaces
    ⍝ route security → Spec.security → public; internal routes use DocsSecurity
    ∇ reqs←_Requirements r
      :If '_'=⊃3⊃r
          reqs←DocsSecurity
      :ElseIf 0≠(4⊃r).⎕NC'security'
          reqs←(4⊃r).security
      :ElseIf 0≠Spec.⎕NC'security'
          reqs←Spec.security
      :Else
          reqs←⍬
      :EndIf
      reqs←,reqs
    ∇

    ⍝ Required scopes for one scheme in a requirement namespace, as a vector of strings
    _Scopes←{s←⍺⍎⍵ ⋄ 0=≢s:⍬ ⋄ ,⊆s}

    ⍝ Extract the credential a scheme definition describes; '' if the request doesn't carry one
    ∇ cred←def _Credential req;type;scheme;auth;in;name
      type←⎕C def ⎕VGET ⊂'type' ''
      cred←''
      :Select type
      :Case 'http'
          scheme←⎕C def ⎕VGET ⊂'scheme' ''
          :If scheme≡'basic'
              :If ~0∊⍴req.UserID ⋄ cred←req.UserID req.Password ⋄ :EndIf
          :Else
              auth←req.GetHeader'authorization'
              :If (scheme,' ')≡⎕C(1+≢scheme)↑auth ⋄ cred←(1+≢scheme)↓auth ⋄ :EndIf
          :EndIf
      :CaseList 'oauth2' 'openidconnect'
          auth←req.GetHeader'authorization'
          :If 'bearer '≡⎕C 7↑auth ⋄ cred←7↓auth ⋄ :EndIf
      :Case 'apikey'
          (in name)←def ⎕VGET('in' '')('name' '')
          :Select ⎕C in
          :Case 'header' ⋄ cred←req.GetHeader name
          :Case 'query' ⋄ cred←req.QueryParams ⎕VGET ⊂(_Mangle name) ''
          :Case 'cookie' ⋄ cred←req.GetCookie name
          :EndSelect
      :Else
          cred←⍬                                ⍝ unknown scheme type (e.g. mutualTLS): the hook reads req itself
      :EndSelect
    ∇

    ⍝ Enforce the route's security requirement.
    ⍝ ok=1: request may proceed, req.User and req.Security are set.
    ⍝ ok=0: req.Fail has been called and body is the error response.
    ⍝ Entries are alternatives (any one must pass); schemes within an entry must all pass.
    ⍝ A hook rejects with 0, or with  [status] auth.Reject body  to choose the status and body.
    ∇ (ok body)←r _Authenticate req;reqs;entry;names;name;i;def;hook;cred;user;sec;saved;status;challenges;challenge;auth;rejection;called
      req.User←⍬
      req.Security←()
      ok←1 ⋄ body←⍬
      →0⍴⍨0=≢reqs←_Requirements r
      saved←req.Response.(Status StatusText Headers)
      rejection←⍬
      called←0                                      ⍝ was any hook called?
      :For entry :In reqs
          sec←()
          ok←1
          :For name :In names←entry.⎕NL ¯2
              i←(_Mangle¨_security[;1])⍳⊂name
              (def hook)←_security[i;2 3]
              cred←def _Credential req
              :If 0∊⍴cred
                  user←0                        ⍝ no credential: don't call the hook
              :Else
                  auth←(scheme:1(7162⌶)name ⋄ credential:cred ⋄ scopes:entry _Scopes name)
                  auth.Reject←_Reject
                  called←1
                  user←auth(Handlers⍎hook)req
                  :If (0≡user)∧0≠auth.⎕NC'rejection' ⋄ rejection←auth.rejection ⋄ :EndIf
              :EndIf
              :If DebugLevel 32
                  ⎕←'STARK: auth ',(1(7162⌶)name),' → ',(1+0≡user)⊃'ok' 'fail'
              :EndIf
              :If ok←0≢user
                  sec ⎕VSET ⊂name user
              :Else
                  :Leave
              :EndIf
          :EndFor
          :If ok
              req.Response.(Status StatusText Headers)←saved   ⍝ undo any Fail from an alternative that didn't pass
              req.Security←sec
              :If 0<≢names ⋄ req.User←sec⍎⊃names ⋄ :EndIf
              :Return
          :EndIf
      :EndFor
      :If 0<≢rejection                              ⍝ a hook called auth.Reject
          (status body)←rejection
          req.Fail status
      :ElseIf 400>status←req.Response.Status        ⍝ no hook chose an error status
          req.Fail status←401
          body←(detail: 'Not authenticated')
      :Else
          body←(detail: _StatusText status)
      :EndIf
      :If 401=status                                ⍝ a 401 must carry a challenge; keep the hook's own if it set one
      :AndIf 0∊⍴req.Response.Headers _HeaderValue'WWW-Authenticate'
          challenges←∪{
              def←⊃_security[(_Mangle¨_security[;1])⍳⊂⍵;2]
              t s←⎕C¨def ⎕VGET('type' '')('scheme' '')
              t s≡'http' 'basic':'Basic realm="',Info.title,'", charset="UTF-8"'
              t≡'http':(1 ⎕C 1↑s),1↓s
              (⊂t)∊'oauth2' 'openidconnect':'Bearer'
              ''
          }¨⊃,/{⍵.⎕NL ¯2}¨reqs
          :For challenge :In challenges~⊂''       ⍝ :For, not ¨, which would call SetHeader once on the prototype when empty
              'WWW-Authenticate'req.SetHeader challenge
          :EndFor
      :EndIf
      :If 0=≢rejection                              ⍝ auth.Reject bodies were chosen by the hook; don't pass them to OnFailFn
          body←(status: status ⋄ reason: (1+called)⊃'no_credential' 'rejected' ⋄ body: body ⋄ schemes: ∪1(7162⌶)¨⊃,/{⍵.⎕NL ¯2}¨reqs)_FailBody req
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ Body for a failure response Stark decided on itself: fail.body, or whatever OnFailFn returns.
    ⍝ fail has .status .reason .body and, for authentication failures, .schemes
    ∇ body←fail _FailBody req
      :If 0∊⍴OnFailFn
          body←fail.body
      :Else
          :Trap 0 DebugLevel 1             ⍝ disable trap if bit 1 set (stop on error)
              body←fail(Handlers⍎OnFailFn)req
          :Else
              body←_HandleError req
          :EndTrap
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ auth.Reject for hooks:  user←[status] auth.Reject body  records the rejection in auth and returns 0
    _Reject←{
        ⍺←401
        ~(⊂⍺)∊400+(⍳100)-⎕IO:⎕SIGNAL⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: auth.Reject status must be 400-499, got ',⍕⍺))
        ⎕THIS.rejection←⍺ ⍵
        0
    }

    ⍝ Case-insensitive lookup in a name/value header matrix; '' if absent
    _HeaderValue←{((⎕C ⍺[;1])⍳⊂⎕C ⍵)⊃⍺[;2],⊂''}

    ⍝ Check at Start that every referenced scheme is registered and every hook is callable
    ∇ _ValidateSecurity;all;entry;hook;name;def
      all←(⊂DocsSecurity),{0≠⍵.⎕NC'security':⍵.security ⋄ ⍬}¨Spec,_routes[;4]
      all←⊃,/,¨all
      :For entry :In all
          :If 9≠⎕NC'entry'
              ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' 'STARK: A security requirement must be a vector of namespaces, e.g. ,(bearerAuth:⍬)')
          :EndIf
          :For name :In entry.⎕NL ¯2
              :If (⊂name)∊_Mangle¨_security[;1]
                  def←⊃_security[(_Mangle¨_security[;1])⍳⊂name;2]
                  :If (0<≢entry _Scopes name)∧~(⊂⎕C def ⎕VGET ⊂'type' '')∊'oauth2' 'openidconnect'
                      ⎕←'STARK: warning: scopes on "',(1(7162⌶)name),'" are only valid in OpenAPI 3.0.3 for oauth2 and openIdConnect schemes'
                  :EndIf
              :Else
                  ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: Security scheme "',(1(7162⌶)name),'" is used but was not registered with AddSecurity'))
              :EndIf
          :EndFor
      :EndFor
      :For hook :In _security[;3]
          'Security hook'_ValidateFn hook (2 ¯2) 1
      :EndFor
    ∇

    ⍝ Signal EN 11 unless fn names a function in Handlers whose valence is in valences
    ⍝ (1 monadic, 2 dyadic, ¯2 ambivalent) and, if result is 1, that returns a result
    ∇ label _ValidateFn(fn valences result);res;val
      :If 0=Handlers.⎕NC⊂fn
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: ',label,' "',fn,'" not found in Handlers'))
      :EndIf
      (val res)←11 10 Handlers.⎕ATX fn           ⍝ ⎕ATX, not ⎕AT: ⎕AT gives 0 0 0 for methods of a class instance
      :If (~val∊valences)∨result>res≠0
          ⎕SIGNAL ⊂('EN' 11)('Message' ('STARK: ',label,' "',fn,'" must be a ',(result/'result-returning '),((1+1∊valences)⊃'dyadic' 'monadic'),' function'))
      :EndIf
    ∇

    ⍝ OpenAPI spec generation

    ∇ r←OpenAPI
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_BuildOpenAPI
    ∇

    ∇ result←_OpenAPIHandler req
      :Access Public Instance
      result←_BuildOpenAPI
    ∇

    ∇ spec←_BuildOpenAPI;paths;r;pathKey;schemes
      :Access Private Instance
      spec←(openapi: '3.0.3' ⋄ info: Info)
      spec ⎕NS Spec
      :If 0<≢_security                  ⍝ add registered schemes to components.securitySchemes
          spec.components←() ⎕NS {6::() ⋄ ⍵.components}Spec   ⍝ copy, so Spec itself isn't modified
          schemes←() ⎕NS {6::() ⋄ ⍵.components.securitySchemes}Spec
          schemes ⎕VSET ↓⍉↑(_Mangle¨_security[;1]) (_security[;2])
          spec.components.securitySchemes←schemes
      :EndIf
      paths←()
      :For r :In ↓_routes
          :If '_'=⊃3⊃r ⋄ :Continue ⋄ :EndIf
          pathKey←_Mangle 2⊃r
          :If 0=paths.⎕NC⊂pathKey ⋄ paths ⎕VSET ⊂pathKey () ⋄ :EndIf
          (paths ⎕VGET pathKey) ⎕VSET ⊂(⎕C 1⊃r) (4⊃r)
      :EndFor
      spec.paths←paths
    ∇


    ∇ Start port;code;j
      :Access Public Instance
      code←⎕NS ''
      code.inst←⎕THIS
      code.Get←{inst._Dispatch ⍵}
      code.Post←{inst._Dispatch ⍵}
      code.Put←{inst._Dispatch ⍵}
      code.Delete←{inst._Dispatch ⍵}
      code.Patch←{inst._Dispatch ⍵}
      j←_jarvis
      j.Port←port
      j.Paradigm←'REST'
      j.CodeLocation←code
      j.RESTFailProcessing←1
      j.Debug←+/(1 4 8 16)×1=2|⌊Debug÷1 4 8 16   ⍝ forward bits 1,4,8,16; bit 2 is replaced by Stark's bit 64/2
      :If ~0∊⍴OnErrorFn ⋄ 'OnErrorFn'_ValidateFn OnErrorFn (2 ¯2) 1 ⋄ :EndIf
      :If ~0∊⍴OnFailFn ⋄ 'OnFailFn'_ValidateFn OnFailFn (2 ¯2) 1 ⋄ :EndIf
      :If ~0∊⍴OnRequestFn ⋄ 'OnRequestFn'_ValidateFn OnRequestFn (1 ¯2) 0 ⋄ :EndIf
      :If ~0∊⍴OnResponseFn ⋄ 'OnResponseFn'_ValidateFn OnResponseFn (2 ¯2) 0 ⋄ :EndIf
      _ValidateSecurity
      :If ''≢ThreadMode
          j.DYALOG_JARVIS_THREAD←ThreadMode
      :EndIf
      j.Start
    ∇

    ∇ Stop
      :Access Public Instance
      _jarvis.Stop
    ∇

    ∇ r←GetJarvis
      :Access Public Instance
      r←_jarvis
    ∇

    ∇ r←Routes
      :Access Public Instance
      r←('_'≠⊃¨_routes[;3])⌿_routes
    ∇

:EndClass
